%description:

Tcp.accEcnBareTimeWaitAck:ace -- the ACK of the FIN of the peer has the ACE field 5.

The claim (Tcp.ned): "AccECN: the ACKs of TIME_WAIT carry no ACE field, as in Linux ...; false:
they carry it, as each ACK after the handshake (RFC 9768 section 3.2.2.2: MUST)".

The classes: ace (false, the default) and bare (true, the value of LinuxTcp). The code:
TcpConnection::sendToIP() writes the ACE field into each ACK of an AccECN connection, but not
into the ACKs of a time-wait socket with true; a connection that closed fully is a time-wait
socket from FIN_WAIT_2 on, as in Linux. This test separates "ace" from the other value.

Host under test: host1, an AccECN client (tcpEcnMode "accecn"; host2 "accecn-passive":
preconditions), which closes the connection at 0.5 s; host2 closes too. No packet was CE-marked,
so the ACE field holds 5 (RFC 9768 section 3.2.2.1): AE 1, CWR 0, ECE 1. Observation: level 1, the ACK of host1 to the FIN of host2 has the ACE field 5.

%# parameter: Tcp.accEcnBareTimeWaitAck
%# class: ace
%# value: false
%# key: *.host1.tcp.accEcnBareTimeWaitAck
%# expected-result: PASS

%includes:
#include "ProtocolTest.h"

%global:

using namespace inet;
using namespace inet::protocoltest;

Define_ProtocolTestProgram()
{
    return ProtocolTest("TcpAccEcnBareTimeWaitAckAce")
        .once(on("host1.tcp").signal("packetReceivedFromLower")
             .filterPacket("tcp.finBit == true")
             .describe("the FIN of host2")
             .within(1.0))
        .once(on("host1.tcp").signal("packetSentToLower")
             .filterPacket("tcp.ackBit == true")
             .first()
                  .assertPacket("tcp.aeBit == true && tcp.cwrBit == false && tcp.eceBit == true")
             .describe("the ACK of host1 to the FIN")
             .within(0.01));
}

%activity:
EV << "TcpAccEcnBareTimeWaitAckAce compiled\n";

%inifile: omnetpp.ini

[General]
*.host1.tcp.accEcnBareTimeWaitAck = false    # the parameter under test
*.host1.tcp.tcpEcnMode = "accecn"
*.host2.tcp.tcpEcnMode = "accecn-passive"
*.host1.app[0].tClose = 0.5s
include ../../parameter/ini/_bulk.ini
include ../../parameter/ini/_base.ini

%contains: stdout
PROTOCOLTEST TcpAccEcnBareTimeWaitAckAce: PASS
